# cron-backup.crontab — Phase Scheduler-Resilience-1A (2026-06-02)
#
# Purpose: independent safety net for critical autopilots so a scheduler.sh
# failure (crash loop / FDA denial / Desktop permission issue / etc.) does
# NOT cause a missed-day outage.
#
# Tonight (2026-06-02 ~02:50 ET): scheduler.sh entered macOS-denied crash
# loop after a file edit triggered Desktop folder permission revocation for
# the LaunchAgent. 03:05 ET populator chain was lost. This file prevents
# recurrence.
#
# Layering with scheduler.sh:
#   - scheduler.sh (LaunchAgent) remains the PRIMARY orchestrator. Handles
#     slate fires, sysAudit, caffeinate watchdog, status snapshot autoticker.
#   - cron is the SAFETY NET for the 3 critical nightly autopilots that
#     refresh the calibration loop:
#       3:05 populator chain
#       4:00 grading:backfill-all
#       5:00 audit:nightly
#   - Both can fire — the npm scripts are idempotent (SQLite INSERT OR IGNORE
#     for snapshotPredictions, JSON file mtime-checks for populators, etc.).
#     Double-fires are no-ops, not corruption.
#
# Why cron not another LaunchAgent:
#   - cron runs in user crontab context which inherits operator's FDA grant
#     reliably. LaunchAgents lose FDA when their plist reloads (the bug we
#     hit tonight).
#   - cron is OS-level, ~40 years of reliability. No script-language bug
#     can take it down.
#   - Each cron entry is independent — one failing doesn't block others.
#
# Install (one-time):
#   crontab -l > /tmp/_curr_cron 2>/dev/null; \
#   cat /tmp/_curr_cron \
#       /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/backend/scripts/cron-backup.crontab \
#     | crontab -
#
# Verify:
#   crontab -l | grep CRON_BACKUP
#
# Uninstall (if ever needed):
#   crontab -l | grep -v CRON_BACKUP_v1 | crontab -
#
# IMPORTANT: macOS may prompt for cron Full Disk Access the first time
# entries fire. Grant it via System Settings → Privacy & Security →
# Full Disk Access → enable "cron".
#
# Cron format: min hour day mon dow CMD
# All times in operator's local timezone (the Mac's clock, which is set to
# America/New_York). NO timezone prefix needed inside cron lines.

# ─── 3:05 AM populator chain — refresh MLB stats/logs + NBA team stats ───
# CRON_BACKUP_v1 marker — used by uninstall filter
5 3 * * * cd /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard && (date '+[%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S] CRON_BACKUP_v1 populator chain starting' >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log; npm run populate:mlb-batter-stats >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log 2>&1; npm run populate:mlb-batter-game-logs >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log 2>&1; npm run populate:mlb-pitcher-game-logs >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log 2>&1; npm run derive:nba-dvp >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log 2>&1; npm run populate:nba-team-stats >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log 2>&1; date '+[%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S] CRON_BACKUP_v1 populator chain done' >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log)

# ─── 4:00 AM grading:backfill-all — refresh calibration corpus ───
# CRON_BACKUP_v1
0 4 * * * cd /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard && (date '+[%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S] CRON_BACKUP_v1 grading:backfill-all starting' >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log; npm run grading:backfill-all >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log 2>&1; date '+[%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S] CRON_BACKUP_v1 grading done' >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log)

# ─── 5:00 AM audit:nightly — daily proof report ───
# CRON_BACKUP_v1
0 5 * * * cd /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard && (date '+[%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S] CRON_BACKUP_v1 audit:nightly starting' >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log; npm run audit:nightly -- --no-populators --no-grade >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log 2>&1; date '+[%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S] CRON_BACKUP_v1 audit done' >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log)

# ─── 9 AM - 11 PM hourly MLB slate refresh ───
# CRON_BACKUP_v1
0 9-23 * * * cd /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard && (date '+[%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S] CRON_BACKUP_v1 slate:mlb starting' >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log; npm run slate:mlb >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log 2>&1)

# ─── 4 PM - 11:30 PM every 30 min NBA slate refresh ───
# CRON_BACKUP_v1
0,30 16-23 * * * cd /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard && (date '+[%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S] CRON_BACKUP_v1 slate:nba starting' >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log; npm run slate:nba >> /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/.scratch/cron-backup.log 2>&1)

# ─── Scheduler.sh watchdog — auto-resurrect if dead (CRON_BACKUP_v1) ───
#
# Fires EVERY MINUTE. If scheduler.sh isn't running, launches it as a
# nohup child of cron (which has FDA via user crontab). Bypasses launchd's
# permission gate entirely. Within 60 seconds of any scheduler death,
# this respawns it.
#
# `pgrep -f scheduler.sh` is the liveness test. Quote-escape carefully:
# - `> /dev/null 2>&1` discards pgrep output
# - `||` triggers next command only if pgrep returns non-zero (no match)
# - `nohup ... &` detaches so cron exits cleanly without waiting
* * * * * pgrep -f "/Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/backend/scripts/scheduler.sh" > /dev/null 2>&1 || nohup bash /Users/andrewmoore/Desktop/betting-dashboard/backend/scripts/scheduler.sh > /tmp/sched.log 2>&1 & # CRON_BACKUP_v1 watchdog

# ─── End cron-backup.crontab ───
